import crate::lint::program_walk::ProgramWalk
import redox_ast::Stmt

-- | Walk a statement run and the blocks its statements own — plan 53 leaf 4,
-- | shared by plan 54 leaf 3.
-- |
-- | The run is offered first, then each block a statement owns, so every list
-- | in the program reaches [`ProgramWalk::stmts`] exactly once.
-- |
-- | Which blocks those are is [`redox_ast::Expr::statement_blocks`], whose own
-- | match is **exhaustive with no wildcard**: a new form that owns a statement
-- | block has to be considered there rather than quietly excluded here. Plan
-- | 55 leaf 1 moved the question to the node, because collapsing `StmtKind`
-- | into `Expr` would otherwise have left this crate matching forty-six
-- | variants to name five.
-- |
-- | # One list per call, which is `RDX1003`'s whole definition
-- |
-- | A nested block is a **separate** call with a separate list, so the shadow
-- | lint cannot see across a block boundary even by accident — plan 54
-- | criterion 5, and the boundary decision 4 says must not drift. Nothing here
-- | hands a consumer an outer list and an inner one together.
-- |
-- | # Where this stops, and why that is safe
-- |
-- | Not into the blocks an **expression** owns — `do`, `async`, `unsafe`,
-- | `try` and a lambda body. Reaching those needs an expression walk, which is
-- | the thing
-- | [`unwrap_call_sites`](super::unwrap_call_sites::unwrap_call_sites) refuses,
-- | and the refusal is affordable here in a way it is not there: a statement
-- | this walk does not reach keeps its warning, so the author sees `RDX1001`
-- | beside the pragma they wrote and the gap reports itself. Detection going
-- | wrong the same way would print nothing and look like a clean program.
-- |
-- | The declaration-level pragma covers these cases in the meantime: an
-- | attribute on the enclosing function suppresses its whole span, expression
-- | blocks included.
-- |
-- | For `RDX1003` the stop costs nothing at all. An expression block is a
-- | separate statement list, which criterion 5 requires the lint to be silent
-- | about anyway — `examples/control.sdx`'s `shadowed` is exactly that shape.
export(crate) walk_stmts : &[Stmt] -> &mut dyn ProgramWalk -> ()
walk_stmts stmts walk =
  .stmts stmts walk

  for stmt in stmts
    for nested in .statement_blocks stmt.expr
      walk_stmts (&nested.stmts) walk
  ()
